        // arm64 path previously dropped the return, so a container
        // built by `let mut a = []` + push (historically observed in
        // the now-retired hxc_loader.hexa `dense` rebuild — atlas
        // path now uses compiler/atlas/merger.hexa per @D
        // h_atlas_single_export, 2026-05-22) kept a STALE array
        // header in its slot; after the
        // runtime's arena dirty-slot / heapify relocated the backing
        // on a later allocation, `_build_node(dense)` received a
        // dangling/garbage array → non-deterministic "container is
        // not an array (tag=<garbage>)" — the last aprime_cc
        // self-host fixpoint blocker (interp-retirement #18). Mirror
        // hexa_array_push: store the result back into the container
        // lvalue when it is a storable local/global Operand.
        if s.op == "index_set" && len(s.args) >= 3 {
            // FLEET arm64 element-pack (HEXA_PACK_ESCAPING) — escaping-poly index_set:
            // a typed-prim array operand of unknown packed-ness routes through
            // hexa_arr_poly_set (TAG_ARRAY_I64 → raw stride-8 store; else boxed
            // hexa_index_set). AAPCS64: v → x0:x1, RAW idx → x2 (idx HexaVal payload),
            // item → x3:x4 pair; returns the descriptor x0:x1 → store-back so a copied
            // handle stays coherent (the in-place store also mutates aliases). Mirror
            // of x86_64's hexa_arr_poly_set.
            if _arm_operand_pack_esc(s.args[0], rm) {
                buf = _hv_load(buf, s.args[1], st, rm, "x9", "x10")  // idx → x10 = payload
                buf = _hv_load(buf, s.args[2], st, rm, "x3", "x4")   // item pair
                buf = _hv_load(buf, s.args[0], st, rm, "x0", "x1")   // descriptor pair
                buf.push(_arm64_instr2("mov", _arm64_op_reg("x2"),
                                 _arm64_op_reg("x10"), "index_set: raw idx payload → x2"))
                buf.push(_arm64_instr1("bl", _arm64_op_label("hexa_arr_poly_set"),
                                 "index_set: hexa_arr_poly_set (runtime discriminate)"))
