        // opcode inline-assembly intrinsic — emits a literal `nop` (0xd503201f,
        // encoded by macho_arm64.hexa, shared by the arm64-linux ELF backend) inline,
        // then returns int 0 ({TAG_INT=x0:0, payload=x1:0}) so the call composes as
        // an ordinary expression. 0-arg leaf, same shape as __hx_syscall0 minus the
        // trap. ADD-only: the compiler never calls it → DEFAULT byte-identical.
        // state/rfc_inline_asm.md. reference: Rust core::hint::spin_loop / Zig asm.
