        // RFC inline-asm rung 2: `__hx_asm("<op>")` → int HexaVal 0, the generalized
        // whitelisted named-opcode passthrough (mirror of the x86_64 branch). Opcode
        // = COMPILE-TIME STRING LITERAL (const_str operand) — same literal-template
        // rule as Rust `asm!`/GCC `__asm__`/Zig `asm`. The portable whitelist {nop,
        // pause, fence} maps to the AArch64 hint/barrier {nop, yield, dmb ish}
        // (encoded by macho_arm64.hexa, shared by the arm64-linux ELF backend),
        // gated behind opt-in HEXA_INLINE_ASM. DEFAULT (env unset) or unknown/non-
        // literal opcode → NO raw instruction, just the boxed int-0 no-op. ADD-only +
        // env-gated: the compiler never calls __hx_asm → DEFAULT byte-identical.
