        // x86_64 `__hx_rodata_tab_ptr` special-case. `__hx_rodata_tab_ptr(table_id)` —
        // DEFINE a PRE-INITIALIZED `.rodata` constant table named `rotab_<id>`
        // (contents = `_arm64_rodata_table_spec(id)`, LE doubles) and RETURN its
        // address via `adrp x1, rotab_<id>@PAGE` + `add x1, x1, rotab_<id>@PAGEOFF`
        // (the AArch64 PC-relative materialization, exactly like __hx_static_slot — but
        // the data is initialized rodata, not a zero .data slot). The const_int
